    "text": "mainstreetmediatn.com\nwebsite\nLawrence County, Tennessee\nInvesting in Public Safety: Strengthening LCFR\nBy DAVID MORGAN,\n17 hours agoA situation that put both first responders and the public at risk has been addressed thanks to action by Lawrence County Government. On Aug. 1, Lawrence County Fire & Rescue (LCFR) Director Tyler McDow announced that the non-profit agency can now pay three trained first responders to work weekdays from 8 a.m.-4 p.m., hours when call volume is high and volunteer availability is low.",
